#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:4
msgid "LetterGator | Privacy"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:11
msgid "How LetterGator handles your data"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:14
msgid ""
"This notice explains what information we collect, how we use it, and the "
"choices you have when using LetterGator. We designed the service to keep "
"letter content protected while still letting us run the platform, provide "
"delivery, prevent abuse, and support your account."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:24
msgid "1. Information we collect"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:26
msgid ""
"We collect information you provide directly, such as your name, email "
"address, phone number, address, letter content, delivery dates, recipient "
"details, attachments, account notes, and support requests. We also collect "
"technical information such as device data, log data, usage events, and other "
"information needed to keep the platform secure and reliable."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:38
msgid "2. How we use information"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:40
msgid ""
"We use information to create and manage your account, process and deliver "
"letters, verify addresses, send notifications, provide customer support, "
"detect fraud or abuse, improve the product, and comply with legal or "
"accounting obligations. We may also use aggregated or de-identified "
"information for analytics and service improvements."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:52
msgid "3. Letter content and encryption"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:54
msgid ""
"Letter content is encrypted before it is stored. Decryption is performed "
"only inside controlled application flows when required to render, validate, "
"or deliver a letter. We do not intend for plaintext letter content to be "
"exposed through normal database access alone."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:65
msgid "4. Sharing and disclosure"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:67
msgid ""
"We do not sell your personal information. We may share data with service "
"providers that help us host the application, send email, store backups, "
"process payments, or monitor security. We may also disclose information if "
"required by law, to enforce our terms, or to protect users, our systems, or "
"the public."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:78
msgid "5. Retention and backups"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:80
msgid ""
"We retain account data, letter data, payment records, and support history "
"for as long as reasonably necessary to operate the service, meet legal "
"obligations, resolve disputes, and enforce our agreements. Some encrypted "
"data may be backed up or archived to improve durability and recovery options."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:91
msgid "6. Your choices and controls"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:93
msgid ""
"You can update certain profile details in your account, such as your email "
"address, phone number, and address where available. You may also contact us "
"with questions about your data, request help with account access, or ask "
"about deletion options where legally and operationally possible."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:104
msgid "7. Security"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:106
msgid ""
"We use technical and organizational safeguards intended to reduce "
"unauthorized access, misuse, loss, or alteration of data. No system is "
"completely secure, so you should use a strong password, keep your account "
"credentials private, and notify us quickly if you suspect unauthorized "
"access."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:117
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Contact"
msgid "8. Contact"
msgstr "Contact"

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:119
msgid ""
"If you have questions about this privacy notice or want to contact us about "
"your data, please use the"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/privacy.html:121
msgid "page."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:4
msgid "LetterGator | Terms of Service"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:9
msgid "Legal"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:11
msgid "Terms of Service"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:13
msgid "Effective date: May 18, 2026"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:15
msgid ""
"By creating an account, purchasing credit, or using LetterGator in any way, "
"you agree to these terms. Please read them carefully before using the "
"service. If you do not agree with any part of these terms, you should not "
"use the platform."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:26
msgid "1. What LetterGator does"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:28
msgid ""
"LetterGator is a scheduled letter platform. You can write email letters now "
"and set them to be delivered on a future date. The service is designed for "
"personal reflection, family messages, professional reminders, and other "
"lawful communications where delayed delivery is useful. We may also offer "
"related features such as physical letter creation, attachments, contact "
"tickets, account management tools, and delivery controls."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:41
msgid "2. Account eligibility and responsibility"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:43
msgid ""
"You must be legally able to enter into a binding agreement to use "
"LetterGator. If you use the service on behalf of a business or organization, "
"you confirm that you have authority to accept these terms for that entity. "
"You are responsible for keeping your login credentials confidential and for "
"all activity that happens under your account."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:55
msgid "3. Acceptable use"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:57
msgid ""
"You agree not to use LetterGator to send spam, phishing attempts, malware, "
"harassing content, illegal material, or any message that violates the rights "
"of others. You may only send letters to recipients you are reasonably "
"entitled to contact. You are also responsible for obtaining any permissions "
"needed for the content, attachments, or delivery details you provide."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:69
msgid "4. Pricing, balance, and billing"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:71
msgid ""
"Some letters can be created without charge, while long-term scheduling may "
"require payment from your account balance. Any fee shown before confirmation "
"is the amount you agree to pay when the letter is scheduled. Balances are "
"tied to your account and may be used for eligible service charges, refunds, "
"or adjustments where applicable. We may change pricing in the future, but "
"any change will only apply to new actions after the update is published."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:84
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "Delivery Date And Time"
msgid "5. Delivery timing and limits"
msgstr "Delivery Date And Time"

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:86
msgid ""
"We make reasonable efforts to deliver letters on the scheduled date using "
"automated systems and retry logic. Delivery can be affected by invalid "
"addresses, recipient-side filtering, mailbox limits, third-party service "
"outages, legal restrictions, or technical events outside our control. When "
"possible, we will surface delivery problems in your account so you can "
"review them."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:98
msgid "6. Message content, encryption, and storage"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:100
msgid ""
"Letter content is encrypted before storage and is intended to be readable "
"only through authorized application flows. We do not design the service so "
"staff can casually browse personal letter content. You remain solely "
"responsible for the text you write, the files you attach, and any claims you "
"make inside the letter. Some encrypted letter data may also be backed up for "
"durability, recovery, or long-term availability, including through external "
"archival systems where enabled."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:114
msgid "7. Editing, deletion, and lock periods"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:116
msgid ""
"If edit or delete controls are available for a letter, they may be limited "
"by a lock period or other service rule. Once a letter is locked, it cannot "
"be changed or removed except where the product specifically allows it. These "
"controls are part of the service design and may vary by letter type, "
"delivery date, or account status."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:128
msgid "8. Account, email, and contact information"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:130
msgid ""
"To keep your account and letters usable over long timeframes, we may ask you "
"to confirm your email address from time to time. You should keep your "
"account information current, including your email, phone number, and address "
"where relevant. If you change your email, the new address may need to be "
"verified before it becomes active for delivery or account notices."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:142
msgid "9. Your submissions and rights"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:144
msgid ""
"You retain ownership of the content you submit, but you grant us a limited "
"license to host, process, transmit, display, and deliver it as necessary to "
"operate the service. This includes the technical right to store your letter "
"data, schedule delivery, create backups, generate previews where enabled, "
"and show letter status in your account."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:156
msgid "10. Suspension and termination"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:158
msgid ""
"You may stop using LetterGator at any time. We may suspend, restrict, or "
"terminate access to any account that appears to violate these terms, create "
"security risk, interfere with the platform, or expose us or other users to "
"harm. If your account is closed, undelivered letters may no longer be "
"dispatched."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:169
msgid "11. No guarantee and limitation of liability"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:171
msgid ""
"LetterGator is provided on an \"as is\" and \"as available\" basis. To the "
"maximum extent allowed by law, we are not responsible for indirect, "
"incidental, special, or consequential damages, including delays, missed "
"delivery dates, data loss caused by events outside our reasonable control, "
"or business losses that result from your use of the service."
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:183
msgid "12. Changes to these terms"
msgstr ""

#: letters/templates/letters/terms.html:185
msgid ""
"We may update these terms from time to time. If material changes are made, "
"we may notify you by email, a notice in the product, or another reasonable "
"method. Continued use of the service after the effective date of an updated "
"version means you accept the revised terms."
msgstr ""

